  "lastWords" : "I filled the hole by splitting on `m`, and check_file reports success on the final file, with no errors and no holes left.\n\n```agda\n+-zero-diag ℕ.zero eq = eq\n+-zero-diag (ℕ.suc m) ()\n```\n\n- **When `m` is 0:** the assumption `eq : 0 + 0 ≡ 0` reduces to exactly `0 ≡ 0`, so `eq` itself is the proof.\n- **When `m` is `suc m`:** `suc m + suc m` reduces to `suc (…)`, which can never equal `0`, so Agda accepts the absurd pattern `()` and no proof is needed.\n\nI didn't need `+-comm` or any other lemma, and I left the header, the imports and the type signature unchanged.",
